let props = {};
props = {"feedbackHeadingText":"Reviews","feedbackStatusRejectedTitle":"Uh oh.","addFeedbackIcon":"ugc-threaded-icon-add-feedback","useReviewAdType":true,"signInLink":"\/authentication\/login?regSource=5xb1tu&relativeRedirectUrl=%2Fthick-and-fluffy-pancakes%23scrollToUgc","feedbackStatusRejectedBody":"Your submission does not comply with our guidelines. Please edit your feedback and resubmit.","aggregatedFeedbacks":"{\"averageRating\":{\"average\":4.7192307,\"count\":13},\"averageMadeIt\":{\"count\":13},\"scoreHistogram\":{\"limit\":5,\"offset\":0,\"totalSize\":5,\"list\":[{\"score\":1,\"count\":0},{\"score\":2,\"count\":0},{\"score\":3,\"count\":1},{\"score\":4,\"count\":0},{\"score\":5,\"count\":1}]},\"reviewCount\":41,\"imageCount\":1,\"tweaks\":[{\"id\":\"seriouseats_5346813088\",\"userIdLastFourChars\":\"8953\",\"created\":1586105899000,\"review\":\"I just got a big propane griddle so what better to do for a Sunday breakfast than pancakes.I only had virgin coconut oil on hand so they did have a faint coconut flavor, but still fantastic. A nice golden slightly crisp exterior with a fluffy interior.This has become the new go to pancake recipe for the family.\",\"helpfulCount\":0,\"displayName\":\"jnachtigal\"},{\"id\":\"seriouseats_5346813065\",\"userIdLastFourChars\":\"bb8b\",\"created\":1556035193000,\"review\":\"Hello. Hmm, do you have any recommendations for using whole wheat flour? Maybe not all of it, I am used to making my pancakes with it and I think I'd miss the flavor.\",\"helpfulCount\":0,\"displayName\":\"zombie127\"},{\"id\":\"seriouseats_5346813053\",\"userIdLastFourChars\":\"8788\",\"created\":1553546833000,\"review\":\"Hey Stella, these look and sound great! To accomodate vegan members of the family, can I use a flax or chia \\\"egg\\\" mixture, instead of a regular egg?\",\"helpfulCount\":0,\"displayName\":\"MaryJo\"}],\"feedbacks\":{\"limit\":9,\"offset\":0,\"totalSize\":38,\"list\":[{\"id\":\"seriouseats_6662909700\",\"userIdLastFourChars\":\"7a70\",\"created\":1741018365000,\"review\":\"Can I substitute Crisco for coconut oil?\",\"helpfulCount\":0,\"displayName\":\"Serious Eats Member\",\"replyCount\":0},{\"id\":\"seriouseats_6540384522\",\"userIdLastFourChars\":\"e48d\",\"created\":1725197575000,\"review\":\"This makes some very tasty, fluffy pancakes, but it DEFINITELY does not make 8 servings. I'd add at minimum an additional 50%.\",\"starRating\":3,\"helpfulCount\":0,\"displayName\":\"Benjamin Billick\",\"replyCount\":0},{\"id\":\"seriouseats_6366482219\",\"userIdLastFourChars\":\"6045\",\"created\":1705249904000,\"review\":\"This remains my go-to pancake receipe for the past several years; they are fluffy but still have a delightfully cake-like crumb!My only comment is that with a #12 scoop I only get 4 (good-sized) pancakes from one batch, not 8. This is so consistent it feels like a scaling error, and means that I always pre-make 12 \\\"batches\\\" when doing my periodic prep.These pancakes also freeze exceedingly well, and hold drop-ins (chocolate chips, blueberries, banana slices) easily.\",\"starRating\":5,\"helpfulCount\":0,\"displayName\":\"Jered\",\"replyCount\":0},{\"id\":\"seriouseats_6123904991\",\"userIdLastFourChars\":\"7460\",\"created\":1677336323000,\"review\":\"Another winner, Stella! SO GOOD. The malted milk powder really sets it off.\",\"helpfulCount\":0,\"displayName\":\"Rachel Ekblad\",\"replyCount\":0},{\"id\":\"seriouseats_6099134811\",\"userIdLastFourChars\":\"bd0d\",\"created\":1674677719000,\"review\":\"This is the best recipe I've tried in the last few years for the following three reasons: 1) It totally works. The pancakes tasted great and are genuinely among the lightest and fluffiest I've ever eaten - as advertised. 2) The recipe is super simple, and made even easier by the fact that you can combine the dry ingredients and oil in advance, well in advance. 3) The recipe is completely unexpected. I'd never have imagined using coconut oil in pancakes, but it winds up making complete sense. I'm averse to all forms of coconut flavors, but refined coconut oil lacks all coconut taste and turns out to be a perfect vehicle for the dry ingredients in these pancakes. Kudos to Stella Parks!\",\"helpfulCount\":0,\"displayName\":\"Rex Lafferty\",\"replyCount\":0},{\"id\":\"seriouseats_6098350703\",\"userIdLastFourChars\":\"a87f\",\"created\":1674596693000,\"review\":\"Why the cold egg? Also, should the milk be cold or room temperature? Most things I've read say you should use room temp eggs and milk for pancakes.\",\"helpfulCount\":0,\"displayName\":\"rp17\",\"replyCount\":0},{\"id\":\"seriouseats_5346813093\",\"userIdLastFourChars\":\"030c\",\"created\":1616848454000,\"review\":\"I've made this recipe and the similar one from America's Test Kitchen, many times. I am lazy and I don't like to wash things so I just use a knife or pastry cutter chop\/ cut the coconut oil into the pancake mix and then finish it with my hands. Itt works perfectly the consistency is great. I sometimes add a little more milk though because I don't like how thick these get but hey they say thick and fluffy and they are!\",\"helpfulCount\":0,\"displayName\":\"Hadmo\",\"replyCount\":0},{\"id\":\"seriouseats_5346813092\",\"userIdLastFourChars\":\"7573\",\"created\":1616084588000,\"review\":\"Love this recipe! Any thoughts on how it could be adapted to make corn cakes? Maybe swap out 50% of the flour for yellow cornmeal?Thanks a lot,Aaron\",\"helpfulCount\":0,\"displayName\":\"atm\",\"replyCount\":0},{\"id\":\"seriouseats_5346813091\",\"userIdLastFourChars\":\"20a1\",\"created\":1606013649000,\"review\":\"If you do happen to over-process the coconut oil in the food processer, is there a way to fix it? Could you cool it in the fridge and re-run it in the food processor? Guessing not but trying to see if there's a way to salvage it.\",\"helpfulCount\":0,\"displayName\":\"gb3\",\"replyCount\":1}]}}","numberOfAlterations":10,"addFeedbackCta":"What do you think of this recipe? Share your experience to help others.","type":"review","photoUploadEnabled":true,"reviewTextOptional":false,"reviewSortEnabled":true,"availablePhotoFilterOption":"{\"label\": \"With photo\", \"option\": \"PHOTO\"}","numberOfFallbackAvatars":5,"helpfulEnabled":true,"recipeAlterationEnabled":true,"guidelinesUrl":"\/about-us-5120006#toc-commenting-policy","feedbackStatusPendingBody":"Your submission is currently pending moderation and will be posted soon.","brandName":"seriouseats","regSource":"5xb1tu","defaultReviewSort":"DATE_DESC","readOnly":false,"reviewChipsRequired":false,"myRecipesEnabled":true,"contentGraphEnabled":false,"replyMinCharCount":2,"errorMessageUploadImageSize":"Uh oh. Your photo size needs to be at least 960x960 pixels. Please try again.","linkDisplayName":false,"page":1,"madeItEnabled":false,"reviewLimit":9,"replySortOrder":"asc","showPhotoNextToReview":true,"replyLimit":5,"docId":5137476,"replySortKey":"createdAudit.lastModified","apiBase":"\/servemodel\/model.json?modelId=reviews&docId=5137476","photoUploadRequirementsText":"[\"PNG, GIF, JPEG formats only\", \"Minimum dimensions 960x960\", \"Max file size: 30MB\"]","addFeedbackGuidelinesText":"Check out our <a href=\"\/about-us-5120006#toc-commenting-policy\">Community Guidelines<\/a> about reviews.","errorMessageLoggedOut":"Session Expired. You have been logged out, please <a href=\"\/authentication\/login?regSource=5xb1tu&relativeRedirectUrl=%2Fthick-and-fluffy-pancakes%23scrollToUgc\" rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"ugc-threaded-login\" data-click-tracked=\"false\">log in<\/a> to continue.","errorMessageUploadFileSize":"Uh oh. Your photo needs to be under 30mb. Please try again.","keycloakEnabled":true,"deletedMessage":"This comment has been deleted.","ratingsHistogramEnabled":false,"loadMoreText":"Load More","reviewChipsOptional":true,"reviewChipData":"{\n \"1-star-chips\": [\n \"Did not work\",\n \"Missing steps\",\n \"Missing ingredients\"\n ],\n \"2-star-chips\": [\n \"Confusing directions\",\n \